# The per-call cooldown gate ([IRET.25.5.1]).
#
# Each `cooldown:` call is wrapped in IF(FN_RATE_ALLOW("notify#call<N>",
# d.id, window), FN_CALL(...), null). Two call sites, `svc.slow` (60 s) and
# `svc.fast` (10 s), keyed on `Dev.id`. Every firing also logs, so a call
# held back is visible as a firing with its log line and without its call:
#
#   t=0   a/1  both calls, log
#   t=0   a/2  neither call (same key, both windows open), log
#   t=0   b/1  both calls (another key), log
#   t=11s a/3  svc.fast only (its 10 s window has passed), log
#   t=61s a/4  both calls, log
#
# The vectors RLOW.4.6.6.1_{keyed_per_entity,window_lapses,two_sites} pin the
# gate against the clause; this holds the runtimes to each other.
assert Dev id="a" level=1
pump
assert Dev id="a" level=2
pump
assert Dev id="b" level=1
pump
advance 11000000000
assert Dev id="a" level=3
pump
advance 50000000000
assert Dev id="a" level=4
pump
